    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The drafts are good, but I'm a bit worried about the contrast. It feels like the first section makes tribal tech sound kind of... I don't know, static? Like it's just about survival and \"resourceful\" stuff, whereas the European section sounds like it's actually driving the world forward with \"discovery\" and \"progress.\" \n\nCan we tweak the first section to make it sound a bit more sophisticated? Like, instead of just \"survival,\" maybe we can frame it as a different kind of intellectual approach to the world? I want to avoid it sounding like these cultures were just playing around with rocks while Europe was doing the \"real\" thinking.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
